1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,380
A vCPU count does not tell you how much
sustained compute

2
00:00:03,380 --> 00:00:08,680
a VPS plan allows. Before buying a shared-
CPU server, check

3
00:00:08,680 --> 00:00:12,720
what the provider means by shared and what
its written usage policy

4
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:15,140
permits. Start with the workload.

5
00:00:15,740 --> 00:00:19,180
A small site with occasional bursts has
different needs from a task

6
00:00:19,180 --> 00:00:22,160
that keeps the CPU busy continuously.

7
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:26,320
Do not assume that a quiet test represents
the way your service

8
00:00:26,320 --> 00:00:30,640
will behave all day. Next, read the
documented CPU limits.

9
00:00:31,060 --> 00:00:36,300
Look for conditions for continuous CPU use,
burst rules and the provider's

10
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:38,320
response when a workload exceeds them.

11
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:42,960
If the policy is unclear, ask support a
concrete question about

12
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:45,140
your intended task before paying.

13
00:00:46,240 --> 00:00:49,000
Then separate the plan label from a
performance claim.

14
00:00:49,640 --> 00:00:54,740
Shared resources, dedicated resources and
the number of advertised virtual CPUs

15
00:00:54,740 --> 00:00:56,020
are different pieces of information.

16
00:00:56,020 --> 00:01:00,360
None of them, alone, proves your
application's response time.

17
00:01:01,060 --> 00:01:05,620
Our take: buying a suitable resource policy
matters more than collecting

18
00:01:05,620 --> 00:01:07,920
the largest headline CPU number.

19
00:01:08,140 --> 00:01:12,460
Keep a small comparison sheet with the
plan, policy source, workload

20
00:01:12,920 --> 00:01:17,320
and unanswered question. This is a
purchasing checklist, not a benchmark.

21
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:20,980
We have not run a performance test for this
video

22
00:01:20,980 --> 00:01:24,180
and do not rank providers from an untested
claim.

23
00:01:24,760 --> 00:01:29,620
The description links to the fair-use guide
at vpsdealswire.com.

24
00:01:29,860 --> 00:01:34,080
Use the site to narrow your shortlist, then
confirm the actual plan

25
00:01:34,080 --> 00:01:36,020
terms on the provider's official page.
